# ─── Signing keys and credentials — must never be committed ─────────────────
# The GitHub remote for this project is public. Anything committed here is
# published the moment it is pushed, and deleting it afterwards does not
# un-publish it: the file stays readable in the repository history and in every
# clone anyone already made. A leaked upload key also cannot simply be rotated
# on Google Play without contacting support.
#
# The rules are written per file type rather than per folder, so a key dropped
# somewhere new is still covered.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
key.properties
upload_certificate.pem
upload-key-credentials.txt

# The reset bundle and the archive of it, both by name and unpacked.
/chrnet-upload-key-reset/
/chrnet-upload-key/
/chrnet-upload-key-reset.rar
